{"base_rate":0.39528432732316227,"brier":0.18064549237170596,"bss":0.2442706148398518,"bss_hi":0.32839403727103855,"bss_lo":0.1603659945125647,"chart":{"base":[403.7,178.9],"fp":[360.3,164.1],"lead":"62,286.1 272,277.8 482,255.1 692,226.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.24 — higher than 38% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +23pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 96% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 11%; promised 95% → rained 73%"},"rel":"77.6,419.2 318.7,343 660.3,149.8"},"country":"NZ","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1455755894590846,"ess":451.33372023349835,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Wellington</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Wellington rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>81%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 721 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 5.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.24, ranked 135 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(86&ndash;164) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>211</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>31%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>52%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>216</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Wellington</b> <span class=\"muted\">New Zealand</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;40% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 40% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.24</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>86&ndash;164\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>721 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Wellington &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Wellington\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.174407582938386,376.82464454976304 88.16080000000001,328.61333333333334 153.09506849315068,247.36986301369865 252.79971830985912,141.04225352112675 348.8936,51.97333333333336 409.93500000000006,18.0 409.93500000000006,24.740740740740705 348.8936,115.06666666666666 252.79971830985912,223.07042253521126 153.09506849315068,317.17808219178085 88.16080000000001,372.29333333333335 59.174407582938386,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"238.11650485436894\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"238.11650485436894\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.174407582938386,352.6729857819905 88.16080000000001,314.05333333333334 153.09506849315068,287.26027397260276 252.79971830985912,269.2112676056338 348.8936,192.72 409.93500000000006,88.77777777777777\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 211 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.174407582938386\" cy=\"352.6729857819905\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"88.16080000000001\" cy=\"314.05333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 27%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"153.09506849315068\" cy=\"287.26027397260276\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"252.79971830985912\" cy=\"269.2112676056338\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"348.8936\" cy=\"192.72\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 81% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 216 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.93500000000006\" cy=\"88.77777777777777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(40%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Wellington the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.32) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.06).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>169</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.060</td><td class='num'>21.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>207</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.252</td><td class='num'>11.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.312</td><td class='num'>13.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.318</td><td class='num'>12.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-41.28664,"lon":174.77557,"n":721,"n_cities":216,"name":"Wellington","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0033175355450236967,"n":211,"obs":0.08056872037914692,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.08520000000000001,"n":75,"obs":0.18666666666666668,"sig":true},{"hi":0.39,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.26863013698630134,"n":73,"obs":0.2602739726027397,"sig":false},{"hi":0.71,"lo":0.39,"mean":0.5502816901408449,"n":71,"obs":0.30985915492957744,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9100000000000006,"lo":0.71,"mean":0.8217333333333333,"n":75,"obs":0.52,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9100000000000006,"mean":0.9941666666666668,"n":216,"obs":0.8055555555555556,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.6,"provisional":false,"rank":135,"rank_hi":164.0,"rank_lo":86.0,"reliability":0.02864453201450742,"resolution":0.08812169465637587,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"wellington","station":"","timezone":"Pacific/Auckland"}